<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enver Hoxha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enver Hoxha was the communist ruler of Albania from 1944 until his death in 1985. A founder and first secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/party-of-labour-of-albania">Albanian Communist Party</a> in 1941, he led the Partisans to victory in 1944 and built a Stalinist dictatorship. Breaking in turn with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, he left Albania deeply isolated, and in 1967 he declared it the world's first atheist state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha.jpg" alt="Enver Hoxha" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petrit Kumi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enver_Hoxha_portrait_(colour_correction).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
